  "_notes": {
    "declared_edges": "Hand-carried [producer, consumer] pairs. Steps 13, 13a, 16a, 16b and 16c keep their 1.1.1 context reads (the Trinity steps have no stored links to them yet): M6c retires 13a and M8 gives 16a-16c records with links, and both remove their pairs. [09, 14] and [14, 16] are computed links no annotation carries.",
    "downstream_consumers": "Records which steps actively consume each step's output. Read by 'specdev prompt-context' and by the W595 staleness check of forward replay. The E550 order check of forward replay does not read it: it uses the positional order in 'steps'.",
    "status_write_exemptions": "policy.status_write_exemptions maps a step to field paths whose change alone does not count as a change of that step in forward replay (E550). Read by validation/forward_replay_check.py. Entries 09 and 14 (milestones[].status) name a field no 1.2.0 schema has and do nothing on a 1.2.0 spec; they serve 1.1.1-shaped specs. Entry 16 (plan.milestone_index[].status) is the status of the step 16 anchor row, which 1.2.0 keeps, and is live.",
    "step_metadata": "Per-step declarative metadata. required_spec_inputs is the inverse of downstream_consumers (producers that feed into this step) \u2014 kept redundant for O(1) lookup and consistency validation."
  },
